+**Zoom in to z18 (64×), on any chart.** Every chart goes to the same zoom 18 (`MAP_MAX_ZOOM`); it stopped at z15 (8× on the zoom readout) before. Satellite and OpenStreetMap have real detail all the way in. Past a chart's sharpest tiles it is drawn from them, enlarged: CVFR, CVFR (AIP), Navigation and Low Alt from z13, Helicopters and OpenFlightMaps from z12.
 
 **No data here.** A chart with nothing to draw where the map is says so, once per arrival in an empty area: *"CVFR has no data here: it covers Israel."*, *"OpenFlightMaps has no data here: it covers about twenty regions, mostly in Europe."* It is read from the chart itself, not a list of regions: the Israeli charts by their own frame (offline too) or a missing tile on our mirror; OpenFlightMaps by its empty (fully transparent) tiles; ATS by the sheet's frame. OpenStreetMap, Satellite and World cover the world and never say it. A tile that failed for want of a signal is not "no data", so nothing is said then.
 
